{"name":"Tiger of Mysore","hex":"#ff8855","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tiger","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Panthera tigris, a large predatory mammal of the cat family, indigenous to Asia.","A male tiger; as opposed to a tigress."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A final shouted phrase, accompanied by a jump or outstretched arms, at the end of a cheer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tiger"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tipu Sultan","blocks":[{"text":"Tipu Sultan, commonly referred to as Sher-e-Mysore, was the Sultan of Mysore from 1782 until his death in 1799. He was a pioneer of rocket artillery. He expanded the iron-cased Mysorean rockets and commissioned the military manual Fathul Mujahidin. The economy of Mysore reached a zenith during his reign. He deployed rockets against advances of British forces and their allies during the Anglo-Mysore Wars, including the Battle of Pollilur and Siege of Srirangapatna."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/TipuSultan1790.jpg/330px-TipuSultan1790.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tipu_Sultan","wikidata":"Q10088"},{"title":"Tiger","blocks":[{"text":"The tiger is a large cat and a member of the genus Panthera native to Asia. It has a powerful, muscular body with a large head and paws, a long tail and orange fur that fades to white in parts, with black, mostly vertical stripes. It is traditionally classified into nine subspecies, though some recognise only two subspecies, the mainland Asian tiger and the Sunda Islands tiger."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Bengal_tiger_%28Panthera_tigris_tigris%29_female_3_crop.jpg/330px-Bengal_tiger_%28Panthera_tigris_tigris%29_female_3_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger","wikidata":"Q19939"},{"title":"Mysore","blocks":[{"text":"Mysore, officially Mysuru, is a city in the southern Indian state of Karnataka. It is the administrative headquarters of Mysore district and Mysore division. As the traditional seat of the Wadiyar dynasty, the city functioned as the capital of the Kingdom of Mysore for almost six centuries. Known for its heritage structures, palaces, and its culture, Mysore has been called the \"City of Palaces\", the \"Heritage City\", and the \"Cultural capital of Karnataka\". It is the second-most populous city in the state and one of the cleanest cities in India according to the Swachh Survekshan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Mysuru_Montage.jpg/330px-Mysuru_Montage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mysore","wikidata":"Q10086"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/af/Official_Seal_of_Tipu_Sultan.png/330px-Official_Seal_of_Tipu_Sultan.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/af/Official_Seal_of_Tipu_Sultan.png/330px-Official_Seal_of_Tipu_Sultan.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOfficial_Seal_of_Tipu_Sultan.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Birth_place_of_Tipu_Sultan_in_Devanahalli_05.jpg/500px-Birth_place_of_Tipu_Sultan_in_Devanahalli_05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Birth_place_of_Tipu_Sultan_in_Devanahalli_05.jpg/1280px-Birth_place_of_Tipu_Sultan_in_Devanahalli_05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Birth_place_of_Tipu_Sultan_in_Devanahalli_05.jpg/500px-Birth_place_of_Tipu_Sultan_in_Devanahalli_05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The birth place of Tipu Sultan at Devanahalli","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABirth_place_of_Tipu_Sultan_in_Devanahalli_05.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/War_coat_of_Tipu_Sultan.jpg/330px-War_coat_of_Tipu_Sultan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/War_coat_of_Tipu_Sultan.jpg/330px-War_coat_of_Tipu_Sultan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"War coat used by Tipu Sultan of Mysore.c. 1785-1790","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWar_coat_of_Tipu_Sultan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Flintlock_Blunderbuss_Tipoo_Sahib_Seringapatam_1793_1794.jpg/500px-Flintlock_Blunderbuss_Tipoo_Sahib_Seringapatam_1793_1794.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Flintlock_Blunderbuss_Tipoo_Sahib_Seringapatam_1793_1794.jpg/1280px-Flintlock_Blunderbuss_Tipoo_Sahib_Seringapatam_1793_1794.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Flintlock_Blunderbuss_Tipoo_Sahib_Seringapatam_1793_1794.jpg/500px-Flintlock_Blunderbuss_Tipoo_Sahib_Seringapatam_1793_1794.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A blunderbuss, built for Tipu Sultan in Srirangapatna, 1793–1794. Tipu Sultan used many Western craftsmen, and this gun reflects the most up-to-date technologies of the time.[25]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlintlock_Blunderbuss_Tipoo_Sahib_Seringapatam_1793_1794.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Battle_of_pollilur.jpg/330px-Battle_of_pollilur.jpg?utm_source=en.wik